WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.672
Detections are only as effective as the telemetry supporting them.

2
00:00:03.672 --> 00:00:15.924
Security teams may use endpoint logs, authentication records, network events, cloud telemetry, application logs, email security events, and identity provider data.

3
00:00:15.924 --> 00:00:23.827
Detection engineers need to understand what data exists, how it is collected, how quickly it arrives, and what fields are available.

4
00:00:23.827 --> 00:00:30.771
A detection that depends on data the organization does not collect will fail no matter how carefully the logic is written.

5
00:00:30.771 --> 00:00:32.986
Telemetry also has limitations.

6
00:00:32.986 --> 00:00:40.909
Logs may be incomplete, delayed, normalized differently, retained for different lengths of time, or missing important context.

7
00:00:40.909 --> 00:00:44.241
These constraints affect confidence and should be documented.

8
00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:49.180
Good visibility planning helps teams choose detections that are realistic for their environment.

9
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:59.158
It also exposes gaps that may require new logging, improved enrichment, better parsing, or closer collaboration with infrastructure and application owners.
